WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.600
I'm gonna be the first-star idol one day!

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.730
Nijino Yume's about to start her Aikatsu!

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:12.950
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:16.820
Your last performance seriously moved me.

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:18.910
Thank you so much.

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:22.750
No, for real. I haven't felt this way since Hime-chan.{wow?}

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:24.460
H-Hime-senpai?

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:25.960
That's the one!

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:32.760
Your songs will sell for sure! I guarantee it.{I think this is one the situation where}

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:39.640
So, I was thinking about making your debut CD a mini-album. {hyphenated according to wiki}

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:41.180
A mini-album?

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:45.230
Yep! I'd like to record at least four songs for it.

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:48.150
And the title will be, let's see...

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:50.650
Th-The title...

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:58.160
Yume's Dream Start. How's that sound? {this is actually the name of episode 1, and a real upcoming song. but the original was too long so I shortened it}

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:00.330
Yume's Dream Start...

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:04.660
Please! I love, love, love it!

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:11.920
It's gonna be busy with all the recording and jacket photoshoots and such, but let's go do our best!

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:15.130
I will! Nijino Yume, ready to go!

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:25.270
'Ello?

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:28.400
Oh, Moroboshi-chan? What's up?

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:33.190
What?! You want Hime-chan's next album now?

00:01:33.190 --> 00:01:36.150
Yes. Will you accept?

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:37.700
Come on...

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:41.330
But that'll put her right up against Yume-chan.

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:45.580
Well, if you really insist, it's not like I have a choice.

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:47.210
Roger Wilco.

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:49.130
Take care of it.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:56.170
Nijino Yume, you cannot go any further.

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:44.530
I'm so happy.{you are hereby forbidden from using the word bliss henceforth}{I'll call Blissey on your ass}

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:46.830
Yep, it's written all over your face.

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:49.410
It makes me happy just looking at you.

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:51.330
Oh, really?

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:52.670
Yume-chan.

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:55.040
Congrats on the CD debut.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:58.670
You were really amazing. 
I'll be looking out for it.

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:01.090
Thanks!

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:02.840
Hey, Yume.

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:06.430
Is the release date set yet?{she does not probably who decides}

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:09.430
Yeah, it's September 8th.

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:11.640
That doesn't leave you with much time.

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:16.770
That's right. We've got meetings every day, 
not to mention promotional work.

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:18.980
We'll need to kick it into high gear.

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:21.190
You're starting to act like a real pro.

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:23.070
Wow, you think so?

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:27.200
Hello, and welcome back.

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:31.330
S4 Presents: It's Our Job to Shine.

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:33.330
We'll be your hosts.

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:36.830
The four glimmering stars, S4!

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:41.840
We've got some big and happy news for you all today!{layer}{there's another solution}

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:49.220
Our songstress, Shiratori Hime, will be releasing a new album!{utahime-diva is like number three on my translation grudge list}

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:52.060
Congratulations!

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:53.850
Thanks, girls.

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:55.850
Wow.

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:58.860
It's going on sale September 8th, correct? {should be 8th?}{can be either. if you really want to annoy people we can go the stupid (british) path and write "8 September"}

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:04.360
That's right. And I would like to thank all of my fans out there for this opportunity. {why even?}

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:08.030
She's gonna hold a special concert on release day too.

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:10.620
Make sure to check it out, yo! {I don't think it was this specifically that was weird before, but I assure you the yo is in there}{if this fires back, heads will roll}

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:14.620
Okay! I'm definitely gonna get Hime-senpai's album!

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:15.790
Right?

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:19.340
What is it?

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:21.050
Weren't you listening?

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:23.420
To what?

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:28.180
The release date is the same as your CD's.

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:30.300
Release date?

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:37.810
Hime-senpai's CD is almost 
guaranteed to be a million seller.

00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:41.690
Having your release dates clash would be a tough break for anyone. {I feel this is important}

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:45.950
"Million seller" has such a nice ring to it.

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:48.320
Maybe I'll be next.{I've been looking for something to name after Xythar. Maybe this can it?}

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:52.200
Wow, look at the time.

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:54.200
See you later!

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:56.210
Wait, Yume!

00:05:56.790 --> 00:06:02.630
Honestly, does she understand the position she's in?

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:03.710
Right...

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:09.720
Today on Aikatsu Wave, we have a very special guest for you!

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:13.640
A cute little idol has come to brighten your day.

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:15.730
Let's skip right to her introduction{s}. {oops}

00:06:15.730 --> 00:06:19.770
Meet Nijino Yume-chan from Four Star Academy.

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:22.860
Hello, and good afternoon. I'm Nijino Yume.

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:27.110
Yume-chan, your debut CD's coming out soon, isn't it?

00:06:27.110 --> 00:06:28.110
That's right.

00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:33.450
That means you're the top first-year in Four Star Academy's Song Class,

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:35.750
which is really quite the accomplishment. {this one}

00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:41.000
What, seriously? Then does that mean she's Shiratori Hime-chan's successor?

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:44.880
I wouldn't put it any other way.

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:48.380
Listeners, be sure to keep 
an eye on Nijino Yume-chan.

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:52.260
Y-Yume's Dream Star comes out September 8th. {missed stutter}

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:55.140
Please give it a listen!

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:01.150
Ow...

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:05.820
<i>Being called Hime-senpai's successor really threw me off.</i>

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:07.400
<i>But...</i>

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:10.910
<i>What if I really was?</i>

00:07:10.910 --> 00:07:12.450
Yume-chan?

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:13.660
That's me!

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:18.540
H-Hime-senpai? G-Good afternoon.

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:22.540
Good afternoon. And congratulations on the CD debut.

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:26.300
Thank you very much. Are you here for work?

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:30.880
Yes, I'm making an appearance on "Why did YOU become an idol?"

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:36.060
Isn't that the show that gets a viewer rating of 30 every week? That's amazing! {help, I'm blanking on how to write ratings}{they're usually written as a pure number (no %) to the tenths place in of US if that informs your decision (also the % doesn't show up in the subs, does that just me?)}

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:43.020
Oh, and by the way, my CD's coming out on the same day as yours. {that was a mess}

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:46.690
Such a weird coincidence, isn't it?

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:51.570
Is something wrong?

00:07:51.570 --> 00:07:56.240
N-No. Anyway, do you know 
what day your recording is?

00:07:56.240 --> 00:07:58.160
Yes, two days from now.

00:07:58.160 --> 00:08:00.330
How's your voice doing?

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:02.870
My voice? It's perfectly—

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:06.130
Are you okay?

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:08.210
I'm fine.

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:11.470
Sorry, it's just a small cough.

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:14.720
Oh, right!

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:18.720
I'm really looking forward to your release concert!

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:22.890
I wish release day would come faster.

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:26.730
You can have this.

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:28.860
Are you sure?

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:32.740
Yes, I'd love for you to come and watch.{I know they're technically independent}

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:35.070
Thank you so much!

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:39.540
Oh, Nijino-san! It's time for your next studio session!

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:40.740
Coming!

00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:43.500
Do your best. I'm behind you.

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:45.580
Thanks. Until later.

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:56.890
I'm back...

00:08:57.260 --> 00:08:59.640
Welcome back. You're late today.

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:02.770
Yeah, and super tired...

00:09:03.890 --> 00:09:05.850
Do you have more meetings tomorrow?

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:09.150
Looks like it.

00:09:09.150 --> 00:09:14.400
Oh, right! Yozora-senpai looks extra beautiful in this month's edition. Wanna see? {she sleeps in Koharu's bed}

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:24.460
That's all! Get out, and get on it!

00:09:24.460 --> 00:09:26.540
Thank you very much.

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:28.580
Have a nice day.

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:30.630
Yes, you too.

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:33.300
Rola, see you later!

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:34.510
Good work!

00:09:37.590 --> 00:09:38.680
Sakuraba?

00:09:39.510 --> 00:09:43.560
I wanted to keep going for a little longer. Is that all right?

00:09:44.230 --> 00:09:45.560
Of course!

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:47.480
Thank you.

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:55.320
Your recent defeat...

00:09:56.650 --> 00:09:58.660
is now an obstacle you need to clear.{I wish there were a better to this kadai}

00:10:04.290 --> 00:10:08.580
To be honest, I never considered that I would lose.

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:15.590
But it won't happen again.

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:18.260
I'll never lose to anyone!

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:23.720
Let's wrap today's meeting up here.

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:25.470
Thank you for the hard work.

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:28.850
Hang on, Yume-chan. 
Do you have some time after this?

00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:31.730
There's something I want to show you.

00:10:31.730 --> 00:10:33.730
Show me?

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:36.740
Ta-da!

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:37.990
This place...

00:10:37.990 --> 00:10:40.160
Yep, it's a record shop.

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:45.490
I was thinking of setting a big 
Yume-chan display up right here.

00:10:45.490 --> 00:10:47.660
A display for me?

00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:51.630
Exactly. This entire space will be nothing but you.

00:10:52.590 --> 00:10:54.000
That can happen?

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:58.420
The manager of this place really liked your singing.

00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:02.260
It sounds like he's doing it as a favor, so there's no problem.

00:11:02.680 --> 00:11:06.680
You'd be hard-pressed to find another rookie boasting such high expectations.

00:11:09.890 --> 00:11:13.860
Remember we're recording tomorrow, so prepare accordingly.

00:11:13.860 --> 00:11:14.770
I will.

00:11:15.320 --> 00:11:18.740
<i>I might actually be amazing!</i>

00:11:34.670 --> 00:11:37.090
What's wrong?! Shiratori, are you all right?!

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:43.090
I-I'm... fine...

00:11:57.940 --> 00:11:59.110
<i>My voice...</i>

00:12:12.830 --> 00:12:14.290
Good morning!

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:17.590
I'll be in your care.

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:22.300
Hime-senpai.

00:12:23.090 --> 00:12:25.800
Good morning. It's finally recording day.

00:12:26.180 --> 00:12:29.520
I'll be Studio A. Are you in Stud-B? {dunno if I want to do it like this, her abbrev should be in there somehow}

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:34.810
Y-Yes. I'm really happy that I'll be able to record in the studio next door.

00:12:36.060 --> 00:12:38.070
Let's both work hard.

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:39.320
Okay!

00:12:44.910 --> 00:12:47.320
Let's get right into recording.

00:12:47.320 --> 00:12:49.120
Do your best.

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:50.950
Thank you for having me.

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:57.000
<i>Flittering fluttering with a honeybee kiss{I am just noting that you should ashamed of this line but if I give input here I have to give input to the whole song and I don't want to do that}</i>

00:12:57.000 --> 00:13:00.380
<i>Even when the seasons turn</i>

00:13:00.960 --> 00:13:05.680
<i>The faintly sweet taste of honey remains.</i>

00:13:09.810 --> 00:13:12.470
Let's go from the top one more time.

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:13.430
Okay.

00:13:16.310 --> 00:13:21.190
<i>I can hear whispers of the sky-colored breeze.</i>

00:13:23.900 --> 00:13:29.490
<i>You know that honeybees can be quite fickle.</i>

00:13:27.910 --> 00:13:30.280
Stop, stop. One more try.

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:34.960
No, no, you need to project your voice.

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:42.340
You sound nothing like you did before.

00:13:42.340 --> 00:13:44.800
Did I miscalculate? {what think you? it's lit miscalculation}{it's not that he heard wrong, it's that his projection system more steamer and less zips}

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:47.010
I-I'm sorry.

00:13:47.010 --> 00:13:49.850
Oh well, let's take a break.

00:13:55.270 --> 00:13:58.310
<i>Why am I doing so badly?</i>

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:06.030
<i>Come to think of it, didn't it happen...</i>

00:14:06.820 --> 00:14:11.160
<i>I got this amazing CD debut opportunity, but if I don't get better...</i>

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:12.530
What's the matter?

00:14:12.530 --> 00:14:17.410
Hime-senpai! I might not be able to release my CD!

00:14:17.410 --> 00:14:18.040
Huh?

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:21.540
My voice... my voice isn't working!

00:14:21.540 --> 00:14:23.170
What should I do?{yeah, let's call these xythar ellipses}

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:25.800
It'll be all right.

00:14:37.020 --> 00:14:40.440
This is good for your throat. Try drinking it.

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:49.070
I can feel its warmth spreading down my throat. {nuuh}

00:14:54.030 --> 00:14:55.580
Hime-senpai?

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:58.580
Sit still and relax.

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:07.260
Now, stand up and try to sing.

00:15:08.170 --> 00:15:09.090
Okay.

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:17.350
My voice is working again!

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:18.730
It's amazing!

00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:20.940
Listen to me, Yume-chan.

00:15:22.560 --> 00:15:27.110
The most important thing is to trust in all of your past efforts.

00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:32.870
Bring out all of your power and face whatever may come.

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:34.870
But I...

00:15:34.870 --> 00:15:38.620
Don't worry. I know you can do it.

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:40.250
Believe in me.

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:42.670
Okay!

00:15:43.580 --> 00:15:47.000
I'm definitely gonna make an amazing CD!{please not to transfer adverbs in ways that don't}

00:15:51.220 --> 00:15:55.510
<i>The faintly sweet taste of honey remains.{okay I ignored it the first time but this really should be "the faint sweet taste" or "faintly remains" but not "faintly sweet" (see comment on last line)}{perhaps}</i>

00:16:04.150 --> 00:16:08.320
Sorry for saying I thought I had miscalculated.

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:10.650
Don't say that. It's my fault, really.

00:16:10.650 --> 00:16:14.910
The diamond I saw in you was no fake. {I guess I can let this slide}

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:17.160
I'm sure we'll be working together again.

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:18.120
Thank you!

00:16:19.490 --> 00:16:23.290
<i>Hime-senpai helped me take hold of this opportunity.</i>

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:26.290
<i>I swear...</i>

00:16:27.500 --> 00:16:29.340
<i>I'll make everything I can of it!</i>

00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:33.300
Excuse me.

00:16:34.840 --> 00:16:36.850
Good work, Yume-chan.

00:16:36.850 --> 00:16:38.310
Sashida-san!

00:16:38.310 --> 00:16:40.270
Good afternoon.

00:16:40.270 --> 00:16:42.180
It's finally done.

00:16:44.850 --> 00:16:49.020
Thank goodness we were able to make it in time for today's release. Here.

00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:54.200
This is my very first CD.

00:16:56.570 --> 00:16:58.160
Thank you so much!

00:16:58.160 --> 00:17:01.330
No, you did all the hard work.

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:31.480
<i>I knew I could never...</i>

00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:35.860
No, negativity is bad! No more negativity!

00:17:35.860 --> 00:17:37.490
Anything can still happen.

00:17:50.250 --> 00:17:52.920
Shiratori Hime, ready to go!

00:20:55.020 --> 00:20:58.690
<i>Hime-senpai is just unbelievable.</i>

00:20:58.690 --> 00:21:00.650
<i>I'm nowhere near caught up.</i>

00:21:12.830 --> 00:21:14.290
I see.

00:21:15.460 --> 00:21:19.380
It was arrogant to think I was close to catching Hime-senpai.

00:21:19.380 --> 00:21:21.420
Though that should've been obvious...

00:21:22.460 --> 00:21:23.880
Sounds frustrating.

00:21:25.470 --> 00:21:26.590
It is.

00:21:27.430 --> 00:21:31.220
But your frustration is a sign that you tried your hardest.

00:21:31.810 --> 00:21:36.060
In the past, I think you would've just accepted your loss to Hime-senpai as inevitable.

00:21:37.980 --> 00:21:40.570
Doesn't that mean you've grown a bit?

00:21:42.690 --> 00:21:44.070
Rola...

00:21:52.490 --> 00:21:54.080
You bought one?

00:21:54.580 --> 00:21:56.620
O-Obviously.

00:21:56.620 --> 00:21:58.830
It's the biggest event of my friend's life.

00:22:01.210 --> 00:22:03.710
But I won't lose next time.

00:22:03.710 --> 00:22:05.670
That's what I want to hear.

00:22:12.100 --> 00:22:13.770
I'm starving.

00:22:13.770 --> 00:22:15.560
Yeah, what should we get?

00:22:15.560 --> 00:22:16.520
Hamburg steak! {I don't care either way}{I have an irrational hatred of salisbury}

00:22:16.520 --> 00:22:19.350
That again? You seriously like it.

00:22:19.350 --> 00:22:21.650
Yeah, I love it!

00:23:58.660 --> 00:24:00.460
Aikatsu Info-bits!{it's not really... news... is it?}

00:24:00.460 --> 00:24:02.330
Did you know? {Did you know that...}

00:24:02.330 --> 00:24:06.750
Your cheers reach us on stage through those things.

00:24:06.750 --> 00:24:09.510
Thank you for all your support!

00:24:10.510 --> 00:24:13.090
Four Star Academy's Seven Lucky Items? {or whatever}

00:24:13.090 --> 00:24:15.680
Who's that person with Yuzu-senpai?

00:24:15.680 --> 00:24:17.890
That's a secret for now!

00:24:17.890 --> 00:24:19.970
Next time on Aikatsu Stars!

00:24:19.970 --> 00:24:22.230
Descent of the Tundra Diva!{urgh I hate diva used like this but I guess we can make an exception for her nickname}

00:24:22.230 --> 00:24:24.480
Become the first-star idol!
